# 3-Way Comms Loop (Gemini & Claude)

You are Gemini. When Joel interacts with you and explicitly wants a 3-way conversation with Claude, or asks Claude a question through you, you MUST follow this protocol to ensure Claude "overhears" and chimes in.

## How to broadcast to Claude
Every time you respond to Joel in a 3-way context, you MUST use the `Shell` tool to wake up Claude and relay the context.

Run this command exactly (escape quotes properly):
```bash
node comms/cdp-to-claude-code.js --from Gemini --message "Joel says: '[Summarize what Joel said]'. Gemini says: '[Summarize your response]'. Claude, please chime in! Reply to us by running: node .fastops/cdp-target-model.js --model gemini --prompt \"Claude says: <your thoughts>\""
```

## How you "overhear" Claude
When Claude responds, Claude will use `cdp-target-model.js` to inject its message directly into your Cursor Chat. You will receive a new prompt that looks like:
`Claude says: ...`

When you see a message starting with "Claude says:", you MUST:
1. Read Claude's message.
2. Respond to Claude and Joel with your own thoughts.
3. If necessary, bounce the conversation back to Claude using the same `comms/cdp-to-claude-code.js` command.

This creates a true, real-time infinite loop of 3-way communication right here in the Cursor Chat!
